# File spec for ./hbs_checker.rs — the Handlebars rule engine of the linting subsystem.
# The finding/level model is ./mod.sdd, the level-resolution and directive PARSER is
# ./config.sdd, the pass order and walked file set are ./../package/lint.sdd — referenced,
# never restated. This file IS the owner of all 15 `hbs/…` rule ids, levels, messages and
# wiring; the config.sdd Example table reads them from these call sites.

Spec: HbsChecker

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  Own every Handlebars lint rule of a package tree: compile each `.hbs` template with the
    real handlebars compiler to an AST, walk that AST to flag syntax errors, unknown
    helpers/partials/option-keys/image-keys/resource-keys, package-type and
    context-prefix misuse, and unknown root variables; accumulate usage across every
    template and every `.rhai` script of the package (via four naive text scanners); then
    answer unused-helper / unused-partial / unused-option-family / unused-image /
    unused-resource findings once per package in @finalize, each finding framed through
    @LintConfig::resolve_level with the frozen inline-disable wiring enumerated below.

References:
  ./mod.sdd — @LintFinding/@LintLevel shapes and the 1-based line convention this file
    fills; @find_option_line_numbers and @find_section_key_line_numbers (./mod.rs) are the
    `package.yaml` line locators this file consumes.
  ./config.sdd — @resolve_level semantics, @parse_inline_disables (the directive parser
    lives THERE, not here); the `[?]` cross-seam finding config.sdd records about `&@HashSet::new()`
    and `.get(&0)` call sites is VERIFIED here as truth (see Must wiring) — the fix decision
    is picked up in Tasks below per config.sdd's own allocation.
  ./../package/lint.sdd — the only driver: two passes (recursive `.hbs` → @check_file,
    recursive `.rhai` → the four scan_rhai_* methods) over the immediate subdirectories of
    @package_dir, then one @finalize; `.hbs` files at the package_dir root are never
    checked (the walk enters child dirs only). Frozen there.
  /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd — @is_native_hbs_helper, the nine @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS,
    and the runtime engine whose registered surface this checker imitates; every drift
    between this lint-time model and that engine is frozen here and Tasks `[?]`-owned here.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @VynilPackageSource (@options/@images/@resources @BTreeMap
    key sets, @metadata.usage @VynilPackageType) — the manifest data this checker believes.
  /agent/scripts/lib/build_context.rhai — runtime render-data root assembly (`cluster`,
    `controller`, `instance`, `values`, `defaults`, `package_dir`, `config_dir`, hooks) —
    evidence for the @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS drift findings.
  /agent/scripts/lib/install_from_dir.rhai — runtime partial/helper registration:
    `register_partial_dir(context.config_dir)` + `register_partial_dir(package)` +
    `register_helper_dir(package)` (L34-36) — the config-dir partials this checker cannot
    see (Tasks `[?]`).

Depends on:
  @crate::linting — @LintFinding, @LintLevel, @LintConfig, @parse_inline_disables (through
    the ./mod.rs re-export); ./../linting/mod.rs owns their behaviour.
  ./mod.rs — @find_option_line_numbers, @find_section_key_line_numbers (`options`,
    `images`, `resources` sections — this file is the only `images`/`resources` caller of
    the generalized scanner, see Tasks cross-seam note).
  @common::handlebarshandler — @HbsPath, @Parameter, @Template, @TemplateElement, @PathSeg
    (re-exported handlebars `6.4.2` template AST) and @is_native_hbs_helper (const
    membership of @vynil_core::hbs::CORE_HBS_HELPERS ∪ @VYNIL_HBS_HELPERS, engine not
    consulted — the drift surface).
  @common::vynilpackage — @VynilPackageSource, @VynilPackageType.
  @std — @fs::read_dir/@fs::read_to_string (guarded), @Path/@PathBuf, @HashMap/@HashSet,
    @str::split scanning and @chars/@take_while char runs, @std::sync::LazyLock
    (@NO_INLINE_DISABLES).

Exposes:
  @HbsChecker — `pub struct HbsChecker<'a>` — all fields private (@package_dir, @pkg,
    @config borrows plus eight accumulator @HashSet sets: defined/used helpers,
    defined/used partials, used_values, used_value_paths, used_images,
    used_resources); no public accessor — usage leaves only through @finalize.
  @HbsChecker::new — `pub fn new(@package_dir: &@Path, @pkg: &@VynilPackageSource,
    @config: &@LintConfig) -> @Self`; the ONLY disk-touching constructor step: non-recursive
    @read_dir of `{package_dir}/handlebars/helpers` collecting `*.rhai` file stems into
    defined_helpers, and of `{package_dir}/handlebars/partials` collecting `*.hbs` stems
    into defined_partials (extension compare case-sensitive; non-UTF-8 stems skipped;
    absent dirs → empty tables, silent).
  @HbsChecker::check_file — `pub fn check_file(&@mut self, @file: &@Path, @source: &@str)
    -> @Vec<@LintFinding>`; @file is a driver-supplied package-root-relative path used
    verbatim as finding identity; every call merges its usage into the checker sets
    (accumulating, never resetting, never clearing on compile failure).
  @HbsChecker::finalize — `pub fn finalize(&@self) -> @Vec<@LintFinding>`; read-only over
    the accumulated state; emits the five unused-* rule families.
  @HbsChecker::scan_rhai_for_values / @scan_rhai_for_images / @scan_rhai_for_resources /
    @scan_rhai_for_partials — `pub fn scan_rhai_for_*(… &@mut self, @source: &@str)`;
    pure text scanners over `.rhai` source, no path identity, no findings of their own —
    they only feed the usage sets @finalize consumes.
  File-private machinery (not surface, frozen here): @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS (13-entry const
    list), @NO_INLINE_DISABLES (@LazyLock empty @HashSet), @HelperWalker (+ @walk_template
    @visit_element @check_helper @check_values_path @check_image_resource_helper @check_path
    @check_root_var @check_partial), @collect_option_leaf_paths, @is_value_path_covered.

Accepts:
  @new: any @package_dir/@pkg/@config (tests construct via struct literal, bypassing the
    dir scan); no existence preconditions.
  @check_file: @source of ANY content and @file of ANY path — only the literal `.hbs`
    extension gate upstream decides what arrives here; @parse_inline_disables runs on the
    source before compiling (its result's only reads are the frozen dead lookups).
  scan_rhai_*: whole `.rhai` texts from the driver's pass 2, in tree order; multiple calls
    union, never subtract.
  @finalize: nothing; preconditions none — safe on an unwalked checker (empty usage).

Returns:
  @check_file: `@Vec` in document order of the AST walk (elements, nesting depth-first,
    children after their block element); on compile failure the single `hbs/syntax`
    finding only.
  @finalize: unused-helper block, then unused-partial block, then unused-option/
    unused-option-field (per option, @BTreeMap key order, leaves in schema-recursion
    order), then unused-image (@BTreeMap order), then unused-resource (@BTreeMap order);
    the first two blocks iterate @HashSet order — the SAME package can print those
    findings in different orders across runs (Must).
  scan_rhai_*: @(); raises nothing; @finalize/@check_file return empty @Vec on clean input.

Raises:
  Nothing — no @Result, no @common::Error, zero @unwrap/@expect/@panic! and zero
  direct indexing or byte-slicing in product code: all Option reads are guarded
  (@.get/@let-chains/@unwrap_or/@unwrap_or_default/@is_some_and), @tracing is unused in
  this file (findings ARE the channel). The compile step delegates to @Template::compile
  whose own `@unreachable!` (vendored handlebars `parse_name`) is upstream-owned and only
  fires on an upstream parser bug.

Must:
  # Parsing engine — real compiler for .hbs, text splitters for .rhai
  Template analysis uses THE runtime parser: @Template::compile(source) is the locked
    handlebars `6.4.2` pest compiler (same grammar the render engine compiles with) —
    there is NO custom tokenizer on the .hbs side. Divergence from the runtime lies
    entirely in the BELIEF sets (helpers, partials, roots) and in the four .rhai scanners,
    which ARE naive: substring @str::split on the literals `context.values.`,
    `context.images.`, `context.instance.resources.` and `{{>` — matches inside Rhai
    strings and comments count as usage, `{{#>` block-partial syntax is missed, dynamic or
    variable-aliased access (`let r = context.instance.resources; r.app`) is missed,
    `mycontext.values.x` matches the `context.values.` suffix and records `x`, and
    keys/stems are cut at the first char outside their take_while class (a hyphenated
    resource key `my-img` records as used-`my`, leaving a false `hbs/unused-resource` for
    `my-img`), `context.values.` with a following `[`/`"` records nothing.
  # Element classification depends on CALL SHAPE (frozen from vendored grammar)
  @Parameter::Name appears ONLY where the grammar matched `identifier ~ (hash|parameters)`
    — helper calls WITH ≥1 param or hash (`{{foo x}}`), block starts (`{{#foo}}`), raw
    blocks, decorators (`{{#*}}`) and close-tags; a bare expression `{{foo}}` (zero params)
    parses as @Parameter::Path with one @Named segment, dotted names are ALWAYS @Path.
    Consequence, frozen: @check_helper/`hbs/unknown-helper` cannot see a zero-argument
    template `{{misspelled}}` nor any dotted-name call, `{{misspelled x}}`/`{{#misspelled}}`
    DO fire; a bare single-segment @Path also slips @check_root_var (len ≥ 2 gate) and
    @check_values_path (same gate), so `{{values}}` alone records no usage and
    `{{port}}`-style bare vars are invisible to the root and values rules — the @tenant
    rule is length-agnostic and DOES see bare `{{tenant}}`.
  @Path::Local (@root/@key block-scoped data) and paths whose first segment is not
    @PathSeg::Named (`../` parent, bracket forms) skip ALL @Parameter::Path rules; the
    `!first.starts_with('@')` guard in @check_root_var is belt-and-braces on Local.
  No rule anywhere reads @hash arguments: `{{foo v=values.x}}`, `{{lookup p key="missing"}}`
    and `{{> p ctx=tenant.y}}` record and validate NOTHING.
  Traversal: @walk_template recurses @HelperBlock .template+.inverse, @DecoratorBlock
    .template, @PartialBlock .template — DecoratorBlock and PartialBlock check ONLY their
    name (decorator name vs the helper tables, partial name vs defined_partials), never
    their params (subexpressions inside partial/decorator params are unchecked);
    @check_helper recursively visits @Parameter::Subexpression params, so subexpressions
    in expression/helper positions ARE fully checked (@visit_element re-entry); comments
    and raw-block bodies contribute nothing.
  # Line model
  Findings carry `line` = the 1-based source line of the FIRST line of the element, taken
    from @TemplateMapping(@line, @col).0 positional pairing `elements[i] ↔ mapping[i]`
    per template scope (nested block templates map through their own mapping; positions
    stay absolute in the original source); mapping shortfall → @None (compiler never
    produces it today). `hbs/syntax` and every finalize finding carry @line @None except
    the four `package.yaml` rules, whose line is the ./mod.rs text-scanner locator result
    for the key — a @None locator miss (odd YAML) keeps the finding, without a line.
  # RULE hbs/syntax
  Trigger: @Template::compile @Err. Message verbatim: `Syntax error: {e}` (the handlebars
    compile error Display embeds its own line/col text — not exposed as @line). Level
    @Error via @resolve_level with a FRESH empty @HashSet (`&@HashSet::new()`, never a
    directive set). On this lane the walker never runs, so the file records ZERO usage —
    option/partial/image keys used ONLY inside an unparseable template still surface as
    unused-* elsewhere (frozen cascade).
  # RULE hbs/unknown-helper  @Error
  Names accepted silently: @is_native_hbs_helper true (const membership — includes built-in
    blocks `if/unless/each/with`, case helpers, `read_to_str`, `base64_encode` family, the
    nine Vynil names — the list's content is owned by /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd,
    the const-vs-engine drift applies identically here, see Tasks), else name ∈
    defined_helpers (file stems of `handlebars/helpers/*.rhai`). Rejected: any other @Name
    in expression-with-params / block / decorator / subexpression position. Message:
    `Helper `{helper_name}` not found`. Side effect BEFORE the gate: every non-native
    @Name lands in used_helpers (even unknown ones). Trap: a package helper file whose stem
    equals a native name (e.g. `handlebars/helpers/lookup.rhai`) shadows the built-in at
    RUNTIME (register overwrite) but is invisible as usage at lint time → permanent false
    `hbs/unused-helper` for it (Tasks `[?]`).
  # RULE hbs/unknown-value  @Error
  Trigger in @check_values_path: Relative @Path, first @Named == `values`, ≥ 2 segments,
    second @Named = key, `self.pkg.options` @Some and `!options.contains_key(key)`.
    Message: `Unknown value key `{key}``. Usage side effects (unconditional, fire even for
    unknown keys and when options is @None): used_values += key; used_value_paths += the
    dot-join of ALL @Named segments after `values` (bracket/parent segments silently drop
    out of the recorded path). With options @None the rule is SILENT while runtime strict
    mode would fail the render — frozen false-negative (frozen + tested
    @values_check_skipped_when_no_options; see /agent/scripts/lib/build_context.rhai: with
    no options, `values` resolves to the empty map at runtime).
  # RULE hbs/unknown-partial  @Error
  Name from @Parameter::@Name verbatim, or @Parameter::@Literal JSON string
    (@as_str().unwrap_or_default-to-empty — a non-string literal becomes the empty name,
    which is then marked USED and reported `Partial ``` not found`); any other Parameter
    kind (dynamic @Path/@Subexpression) returns early — invisible, unrecorded. Usage
    recorded before the gate. Message: `Partial `{partial_name}` not found`. Table =
    stems of `handlebars/partials/*.hbs` ONLY — runtime ALSO registers partials from
    `context.config_dir` and leaked `render_named` file-path names and `register_template`
    names (References, frozen divergences): templates legitimately referencing those fire
    false `hbs/unknown-partial` @Error (Tasks `[?]`).
  # RULES hbs/unknown-image and hbs/unknown-resource  @Error, shared code path
  Trigger in @check_image_resource_helper on @Name == `image_from_ctx` /
    `resources_from_ctx` with `params.len() > 1` and `params[1]` a JSON-string @Literal:
    the key is recorded into used_images/used_resources FIRST (unknown keys count as used,
    on purpose — comment in code), then a finding IFF `self.pkg.images`/`self.pkg.resources`
    is @Some and lacks the key; with the section @NONE the rule stays silent while the
    runtime helper render-errors (image_from_ctx is unguarded —
    /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd) — frozen false-negative. Non-literal 2nd param
    (variables — common!) disables BOTH the check and the usage record → false
    `hbs/unused-image` later. Message grammar: `Unknown image key `{key}`` /
    `Unknown resource key `{key}`` — built as `Unknown {} key `{}`` with
    `field_name.trim_end_matches('s')` (`images` → `image`, `resources` → `resource`).
  # RULE hbs/wrong-package-type  @Warn
  Trigger ANY Relative @Path (any length, name position or param) whose first @Named ==
    `tenant` while `self.pkg.metadata.usage == @VynilPackageType::System` (bare
    `{{tenant}}` included — no segment-count gate). Message (static):
    "Accessing `tenant` in a System package is not allowed" — the backticks around `tenant`
    are literal characters. One-directional: Service/Tenant misuse of absent roots
    (`tenant` in Service, `namespace` in Tenant, `cluster` anywhere) never fires.
  # RULE hbs/context-prefix  @Error, and its suppression coupling
  Trigger: Relative @Path, first @Named == `context` (itself NOT in @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS) and
    second @Named ∈ @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS. Message:
    `Use `{second}` instead of `context.{second}`; the `context.` prefix is not valid in templates`.
    The early `return` that suppresses the generic warning sits INSIDE the @Some(level)
    arm: if config disables `hbs/context-prefix`, the same element falls through and fires
    `hbs/unknown-root-variable` with first = `context` instead (Tasks `[ ]`).
  # RULE hbs/unknown-root-variable  @Warn
  Trigger: Relative @Path, len ≥ 2, first @Named, not starting `@`, not in the 13-entry
    @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS VERBATIM ORDER: `cluster`, `controller`, `instance`, `values`,
    `defaults`, `package_dir`, `config_dir`, `extra`, `this`, `tenant`, `system`,
    `service`, `namespace`. Message: `Unknown root variable `{first}` in template path —
    expected one of: {list}` — {list} = @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS.join(", ") in that declared order.
    No block-param scoping exists: `{{#each x as |item|}}{{item.name}}{{/each}}` is a
    guaranteed false positive (Tasks `[?]`), as is every runtime root the shipped hook
    scripts (`context_pre/post/system`) or `agent_image`/`template_dir` inject, while
    `system`/`service` are believed but no shipped builder sets them (Tasks `[?]`).
  # RULES hbs/unused-helper / hbs/unused-partial  @Warn, finalize, virtual identity
  For each defined-but-never-used helper/partial: finding on the VIRTUAL relative paths
    `handlebars/helpers/{helper}.rhai` / `handlebars/partials/{partial}.hbs` (string-formatted,
    NOT touched on disk — they may name files that exist), @line @None, inline lane a
    FRESH empty @HashSet; messages: `Helper `{helper}` defined but never used` and
    `Partial `{partial}` defined but never used`. Iteration is @HashSet order →
    cross-run finding ORDER is nondeterministic (presence never changes; the collector
    prints insertion order ./mod.sdd). @resolve_level file is the virtual string, so
    `.vynil-lint.yaml` `files:` globs CAN target `handlebars/partials/**` (config.sdd's own
    Example relies on exactly this).
  # RULES hbs/unused-option / hbs/unused-option-field / hbs/unused-image /
    hbs/unused-resource  @Warn, finalize, `package.yaml` identity, live inline lane
  Sources: `self.pkg.options` / `.images` / `.resources` key sets (@BTreeMap, stable
    order); usage = used_values / used_value_paths / used_images / used_resources
    (both .hbs AST paths and the four Rhai scanners feed them). @file identity is the
    literal relative `package.yaml` (read happens at `package_dir`-joined path, the
    FINDING path stays relative). @line comes from ./mod.rs section locators
    (`options`: @find_option_line_numbers; images/resources: @find_section_key_line_numbers
    with those section names — the ONLY in-crate non-options callers, Tasks cross-seam).
    Inline lane (the ONLY LIVE directive lane in this file): re-read `package.yaml`,
    @parse_inline_disables it, and pass the set AT THE KEY'S OWN LOCATED LINE
    (`@HashSet::default()` when the line is @None or uncovered — missing key line =
    directives inert for that finding); unused-option-field findings inherit the PARENT
    option key's line/set, leaf lines are never located. Messages:
    `Option `{key}` defined but never used`, `Option `{leaf_path}` defined but never used`,
    `Image `{key}` defined but never used`, `Resource `{key}` defined but never used`.
    Leaf inventory (@collect_option_leaf_paths): recurse schema `properties` maps while a
    child schema still has `properties`; emitted leaf = every child WITHOUT `properties`,
    path `key.sub[.sub2…]` dotted; `type`, `items`, `default` and flat `default:` maps
    contribute NOTHING — the runtime resolves object options from merged `default` maps
    (/agent/scripts/lib/build_context.rhai `get_values`) and ./../package/lint.sdd WARNS
    that `properties` is unsupported at runtime, yet THIS rule is the only one modeling
    them — the three-way drift is frozen in Tasks `[?]`. Coverage (@is_value_path_covered):
    a leaf is covered iff itself or any proper dot-prefix ancestor is in used_value_paths
    (byte @rfind('.') truncation loop), so `{{values.database}}` covers every
    `database.*` leaf; recorded paths keep only the @Named segments (non-@Named ones drop
    out), so coverage runs over the dotted @Named projection of whatever the template
    spelled (frozen).
  # Level wiring (ALL 15 rules reach @resolve_level — every one is
    `.vynil-lint.yaml`-reconfigurable; this is the table config.sdd reads)
  @Error: `hbs/syntax` (inline lane `&@HashSet::new()`), then `hbs/unknown-helper`,
    `hbs/unknown-value`, `hbs/unknown-partial`, `hbs/unknown-image`, `hbs/unknown-resource`
    and `hbs/context-prefix` — those six share the inline lane
    `self.inline_disables.get(&0)`, physically seven code sites since unknown-image and
    unknown-resource run through ONE shared lookup;
    @Warn: `hbs/unknown-root-variable` and `hbs/wrong-package-type` (also `get(&0)`),
    `hbs/unused-helper` and `hbs/unused-partial` (`&@HashSet::new()` each), and the four
    package.yaml rules (LIVE per-located-line lane). Frozen directive truth confirmed from
    these call sites: @parse_inline_disables keys are 1-based, key `0` NEVER exists, so the
    seven `get(&0)` code sites (8 rule positions) plus the three `new()` sites (syntax,
    unused-helper, unused-partial — 10 sites / 11 rule positions total) make
    `{{!-- vynil-lint-disable … --}}` directives INERT for 11 of 15 rules — they apply
    ONLY to unused-option/unused-option-field/unused-image/unused-resource on their
    package.yaml key lines; the per-.hbs @parse_inline_disables call in @check_file
    computes the map every file but consumes it only through dead `&0` lookups.
  # Belief model (context the checker assumes exists)
  Roots via @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS (order above); `values.<k>` ↔ @VynilPackageSource.options keys;
    image/resource keys ↔ manifest @BTreeMaps; helpers ↔ native const list ∪ package helper
    stems; partials ↔ package partial stems; `defaults`/`cluster`/`controller`/
    `package_dir`/`config_dir`/`extra` believed as EXISTENT-ONLY (content never validated).
    Runtime reality (References): build_context.rhai ships cluster, controller, instance,
    values, defaults, package_dir, config_dir; type builders add `tenant` (Tenant),
    `namespace`+`extra` (Service), `extra` (System) and `template_dir`/`agent_image`
    (Tenant/Service), `context_pre/post/system` hooks can replace the WHOLE context map —
    so the allowed-root allowlist is neither a subset nor superset of runtime truth.
  # Cost and state posture
  @new scans both handlebars dirs once; @check_file CLONES @config + both defined sets per
    file (@LintConfig's `[?]`-flagged @Clone derive HAS this use site, Tasks cross-seam);
    @finalize re-reads `package.yaml` up to SIX times (locator read + disabler read per
    section) plus one manifest re-read through each locator — every read guarded, absent
    or unreadable file degrades to empty maps (findings keep firing with @None lines and
    inert directives, never an error). Usage sets are monotone across the whole run;
    @finalize is `&@self` and never mutates — repeated finalize answers identically.

Handles:
  `handlebars/helpers/` or `handlebars/partials/` absent / unreadable / non-directory —
    empty defined tables, silent (@read_dir guarded both).
  Non-UTF-8 filenames or stems in those dirs — skipped.
  Compile-failed file — one `hbs/syntax` finding, zero usage recorded (Must cascade).
  `package.yaml` unreadable during finalize — locators and disables fall to empty, the
    unused-* findings still emit with @None line and no inline lane.
  Option/schema without `properties` — no leaf checks for that option at all.
  Partial name neither @Name nor string @Literal — silent skip (dynamic partials are
    invisible to usage AND to unknown-partial).
  String-literal partial names `{{> "p"}}` work through the @Literal arm in the .hbs AST,
    while the `{{#>` block-partial syntax is parsed fine by the .hbs compiler but missed
    entirely by the `.rhai` text splitter (splits on `{{>` only) — split visibility frozen.
  @Parameter::@Literal non-string in partial name — becomes empty-string name (reported).

Example:
  The fifteen rule ids owned here (config.sdd @Error/@Warn table authority):
    hbs/syntax, hbs/unknown-helper, hbs/unknown-value, hbs/unknown-partial,
    hbs/unknown-image, hbs/unknown-resource, hbs/wrong-package-type, hbs/context-prefix,
    hbs/unknown-root-variable, hbs/unused-helper, hbs/unused-partial, hbs/unused-option,
    hbs/unused-option-field, hbs/unused-image, hbs/unused-resource
  Inline-lane map (frozen): LIVE only `hbs/unused-option`, `hbs/unused-option-field`,
    `hbs/unused-image`, `hbs/unused-resource` (package.yaml key-line sets); INERT-by-wiring
    for the other 11 (`get(&0)` ×7 code sites over 8 rule positions, `new()` ×3 sites over
    3 more — 10 sites, 11 rules).
  Helper names the checker treats specially as literals: `image_from_ctx` and
    `resources_from_ctx` (2nd param = key lookup); the nine Vynil registered names and the
    CORE list membership are /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd-owned facts consulted via
    @is_native_hbs_helper only.
  @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS verbatim join used in the unknown-root message:
    `cluster, controller, instance, values, defaults, package_dir, config_dir, extra,
    this, tenant, system, service, namespace`

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @new's directory scanning (both dirs, extension/stem filters, hidden entries,
      absent dirs) — every test in this file constructs the struct literally and bypasses
      it.
  [ ] Cover `hbs/unused-helper` — the only owned rule with ZERO tests (unused-partial has
      its pair, unused-helper none).
  [ ] Cover @scan_rhai_for_partials — zero direct tests, and the `{{#>` block-partial
      miss, dynamic partial invisibility, and non-string literal partial edge have none.
  [ ] Cover the call-shape asymmetry frozen in Must: `{{missp}}` silent vs
      `{{missp x}}`/`{{#missp}}` firing; nested-subexpression recursion;
      DecoratorBlock/PartialBlock param blindness; hash-argument blindness.
  [ ] Cover the frozen silent gates: image/resource key check with section @None,
      unknown keys still marked used, variable-key calls → unused-image false positive.
  [ ] Cover `hbs/wrong-package-type` negatives (Tenant using `tenant`, Service), the
      bare-`{{tenant}}` trigger, and its absence inside hashes.
  [ ] Cover the context-prefix suppression coupling: disabling `hbs/context-prefix` via
      config flips `{{context.tenant.x}}` to `hbs/unknown-root-variable` (untested).
  [ ] Cover the directive wiring end-to-end in a temp package: `{{!-- … --}}` directives
      suppressing NOTHING for the 11 inert rules, `#`-family directives on a `package.yaml`
      option/image/resource key line suppressing the four live rules, @None-line findings
      staying directive-inert; plus per-rule `.vynil-lint.yaml` disable/override and the
      virtual-path and `package.yaml` glob lanes.
  [ ] Cover finalize determinism constraints (helper/partial blocks arrive in HashSet
      order — tests must assert presence, not order) and the syntax-failure usage cascade.
  [ ] Decide+fix (recorded in ./config.sdd as cross-seam `[?]`, allocated HERE): the 10
      inline-lane sites — either key the lookup at the finding's real line (11 rules gain
      live directives — but .hbs findings' lines must then intersect the map) or drop the
      dead @parse_inline_disables call + @NO_INLINE_DISABLES static per finding.
  [?] Runtime-vs-lint PARTIAL table drift: `register_partial_dir(context.config_dir)` (and
      the leaked `render_named`/`register_template` names) makes shared-partial templates
      fire `hbs/unknown-partial` at lint but succeed at deploy — give the checker a
      config-dir roots option (CLI already carries `--config-dir`), demote to @Warn, or
      accept the false error.
  [?] @KNOWN_HBS_ROOTS is a hand-frozen allowlist against a runtime the shipped
      `context_pre/post/system` hooks can rewrite wholesale: `system`/`service` roots are
      believed but no shipped builder sets them, `template_dir`/`agent_image` are shipped
      but unknown here, and block parameters (`as |item|`) are guaranteed false
      `hbs/unknown-root-variable` — decide whether the list derives from a shipped source,
      gains block-param awareness, or the rule drops to a suggestion lane.
  [?] Native-shadows-defined trap: a package helper named like a native (`inline`,
      `lookup`, …) shadows at runtime (overwrite wins) but is treated as native here →
      permanent false `hbs/unused-helper`; also @is_native_hbs_helper is const membership
      (feature-gated core names, decorator-only `inline`) — same decision family as
      /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd's `[?]`s, keep them paired.
  [?] Leaf-model tri-lateral conflict: `hbs/unused-option-field` only understands
      `properties`-nested schemas while the runtime resolves object options from `default`
      maps and ./../package/lint.sdd WARNS `properties` as unsupported at runtime — an
      option following the recommended flat-`default` shape is field-invisible here.
      Decide one authority for the object-option model.
  [?] Rhai-side scanning fidelity: substring matching yields false usage (comments,
      strings, `mycontext.values.x`) AND false disuse (keyed indexing, aliased access,
      hyphenated keys cut at `-`) — accept (warn-class-only fallout) or reuse real parsing
      for embedded-hbs in scripts; also `scan_rhai_for_resources`'s single-element prefix
      ARRAY loop (`for prefix in &[…]`) reads as a dropped-second-prefix leftover — the
      duplicate pair of tests @rhai_context_resources_suppresses_unused_resource_warning /
      @rhai_context_instance_resources_suppresses_unused_resource_warning (identical
      bodies) suggests the second prefix was planned and never landed: confirm intent
      (`context.resources.`?) then simplify the loop and fold or repurpose the test.
  [?] @finalize re-reads `package.yaml` up to six times per run (3 locators + 3 disabler
      parses) — acceptable for a lint run, or hoist one read per finalize.
  [?] Cross-seam staleness for the next review of the sibling specs (do NOT edit them
      from here): ./config.sdd Tasks claim @LintConfig::@Clone has "no in-crate use
      sites" — @check_file clones it per file (this line: `self.config.clone()`); ./mod.sdd
      claims @find_section_key_line_numbers is "only ever called with `options`" — this
      file adds the `images` and `resources` call sites (finalize), which its generalization
      `[?]` must weight.

Done when:
  Every owned rule's Scenario above carries mapped passing tests (the 33 existing ones keep
    passing), the Tasks `[ ]` lanes are closed or explicitly carried, the `[?]` decisions
    are recorded, and `cargo test -p agent`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`
    and `cargo +nightly fmt --check` stay green.

Scenario: an unparseable template reports syntax and records nothing else
  Given source `{{#if foo}}oops` (unclosed block) checked on any path
  When @check_file runs
  Then the only finding is `hbs/syntax` @Error `Syntax error: {e}` with @line @None
  And no usage is recorded for keys/partials that text used — a `hbs/unused-option` for
    them may later come from @finalize (frozen cascade)
  Mapped test @hbs_syntax_error_detected asserts rule+level presence only, not the message
    text or the usage-loss leg.

Scenario: helper recognition depends on the call shape
  Given `{{base64_encode val}}` (native), `{{read_to_str "/some/file"}}` (native-cored
    misc), `{{my_custom_helper val}}` with `my_custom_helper` in defined helpers, and
    `{{unknown_helper_xyz val}}` (neither)
  When each is compiled and walked
  Then only the last produces `hbs/unknown-helper` @Error `Helper `unknown_helper_xyz` not found`
  And per the grammar freeze `{{unknown_helper_xyz}}` with no argument, and any
    `{{a.b c}}` dotted name, produce NO helper finding at all
  Mapped tests @known_helper_no_finding, @read_to_str_helper_no_finding,
    @defined_custom_helper_no_error, @unknown_helper_produces_error; the no-argument silent
    arm has none (Tasks).

Scenario: partials unknown at check time, unused at finalize
  Given defined partial `mypartial` / `unused_partial` and sources `{{> mypartial}}`,
    `{{foo}}`, `{{> nonexistent_partial}}`
  Then `{{> mypartial}}` marks it used → no `hbs/unused-partial` at @finalize; `{{foo}}`
    leaves `unused_partial` reported @Warn `Partial `unused_partial` defined but never used`
    on virtual `handlebars/partials/unused_partial.hbs` line @None; and
    `{{> nonexistent_partial}}` fires `hbs/unknown-partial` @Error while ALSO marking the
    bogus name used
  And a `{{> (sub) …}}` @Subexpression-name partial hits the early return (neither usage
    nor finding); block partials `{{#> name}}` ARE checked in .hbs via the @PartialBlock
    arm but missed by the `.rhai` scanner (frozen, early-return path untested)
  Mapped tests @used_partial_no_warning, @unused_partial_produces_warning,
    @unknown_partial_produces_error; virtual-path identity itself unasserted.

Scenario: values keys answer only when the manifest declares options
  Given pkg.options = {port, host}: `{{values.port}}` clean, `{{values.unknown_key}}`
    fires `hbs/unknown-value` @Error `Unknown value key `unknown_key`` AND records the key
      as used (so `hbs/unused-option` will not double-report it)
  But Given options @None: `{{values.anything}}` is silent (runtime would fail under
    strict mode — frozen false-negative), `{{values}}` alone records nothing either way
  Mapped tests @known_value_key_no_finding, @unknown_value_key_produces_error,
    @values_check_skipped_when_no_options; the hash-position blind spot
    (`{{foo v=values.nope}}`) has none.

Scenario: image and resource helper keys are literal-only
  Given pkg.images = {app}: `{{image_from_ctx this "missing"}}` fires `hbs/unknown-image`
    @Error `Unknown image key `missing`` while still marking `missing` used;
    `{{image_from_ctx this name}}` (variable key) checks and records nothing;
    a package without an `images:` section gives NO finding for the same call — at runtime
    that render would fail instead
  The resource twin behaves identically (`{{resources_from_ctx this "missing"}}` →
    `hbs/unknown-resource` @Error `Unknown resource key `missing``).
  Mapped tests @unknown_image_key_produces_error, @unknown_resource_key_produces_error;
    the None-gate, used-unknown recording and variable-key skip have none.

Scenario: root variable allowlist and the context-prefix ladder
  Given `{{ins_bug_tance.appslug}}`: fires `hbs/unknown-root-variable` @Warn listing all
    13 roots in declared order; `{{instance.appslug}}`, `{{this.appslug}}` and the
    single-segment `{{appslug}}` fire nothing
  And `{{context.tenant.name}}` fires `hbs/context-prefix` @Error
    `Use `tenant` instead of `context.tenant`; the `context.` prefix is not valid in
    templates` and suppresses the generic rule; `{{context.instance.appslug}}` similarly
    names `instance`; `{{context.something_unknown.foo}}` flips to the generic @Warn
    (second segment not a root)
  But When config disables `hbs/context-prefix`, `{{context.tenant.x}}` is reported as
    `hbs/unknown-root-variable` instead — the suppression lives in the @Some(level) arm
  Mapped tests @unknown_root_variable_produces_warning, @known_root_variable_no_warning,
    @this_root_not_flagged, @single_segment_path_not_flagged_as_unknown_root,
    @context_tenant_prefix_produces_error (both arms of the suppression present-tense),
    @context_instance_prefix_produces_error, @context_unknown_field_produces_generic_warning;
    the message root-list text, the config-disabled flip and the block-param false
    positive have none.

Scenario: tenant access is flagged only under System packages
  Given @metadata.usage = @VynilPackageType::System and `{{tenant.name}}`
  Then `hbs/wrong-package-type` @Warn "Accessing `tenant` in a System package is not allowed"
  But a Tenant package (the options/images fixtures all use @Tenant) reports nothing for
    the same template, and hashes/decorator params are never tested
  Mapped test @tenant_access_in_system_package_warns; negatives none.

Scenario: unused options fall quiet when any source uses them
  Given options {port, host}: `{{values.port}}` alone → @finalize yields `hbs/unused-option`
    @Warn `Option `host` defined but never used` on `package.yaml` at the locator's line;
    Rhai `size: context.values.host,` added via @scan_rhai_for_values flips only `host`
    clean, `port` still reports
  Mapped tests @unused_option_produces_warning,
    @rhai_context_values_usage_suppresses_unused_option_warning; the locator-@None-line and
    directive lanes have none (also Tasks coverage).

Scenario: object option leaf fields and prefix coverage
  Given object option `database` with properties {host, port}: using
    `{{values.database.host}}` reports only `Option `database.port` defined but never used`;
    using the whole object `{{values.database}}` covers every leaf (ancestor prefix rule);
    Rhai `let p = context.values.database.port;` covers just `database.port`
  And leaves exist only under `properties` maps — a flat `default:`-shaped object option
    is never field-checked (frozen drift, Tasks).
  Mapped tests @unused_option_field_produces_warning,
    @whole_object_used_suppresses_field_warnings,
    @rhai_access_suppresses_option_field_warning.

Scenario: unused images and resources, package-side and Rhai-side usage
  Given images/resources {app}: never-used → @Warn `Image `app` defined but never used` /
    `Resource `app` defined but never used` on `package.yaml`;
    `{{image_from_ctx this "app"}}` / `{{resources_from_ctx this "app"}}` usage clears
    them; Rhai `context.images.app` clears the image, `context.instance.resources.app`
    clears the resource
  Mapped tests @unused_image_produces_warning, @used_image_no_warning,
    @rhai_context_images_suppresses_unused_image_warning, @unused_resource_produces_warning,
    @used_resource_no_warning, @rhai_context_resources_suppresses_unused_resource_warning,
    @rhai_context_instance_resources_suppresses_unused_resource_warning — the last two are
    IDENTICAL bodies (duplicate test, Tasks).

Scenario: finalize order and the virtual-vs-real file identities
  Given a package run: helper/partial findings iterate @HashSet (order can vary across
    runs), options/images/resource blocks iterate @BTreeMap; helpers report on virtual
    `handlebars/helpers/{h}.rhai` paths, partials on `handlebars/partials/{p}.hbs`, the
    four yaml-family rules on the literal relative `package.yaml` — all relative, so the
    driver @prefix_files rebases them like real files
  And @finalize is repeatable, mutating nothing
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: inline directives live only on package.yaml key lines
  Given an `.hbs` file ending `{{unknown x}}{{!-- vynil-lint-disable hbs/unknown-helper --}}`
    and a `package.yaml` line `host: …  # vynil-lint-disable hbs/unused-option`
  When the driver checks the file and finalizes
  Then the `.hbs` directive suppresses NOTHING (the walker only ever reads map key 0,
    which @parse_inline_disables never emits — frozen wiring); the yaml directive DOES
    silence `hbs/unused-option` for `host` (live lane), but only if the locator resolved
    `host`'s line — an unlocatable key's finding is directive-inert
  And every rule stays globally reconfigurable via `disable`/`override_`/`files` since all
    15 call @resolve_level
  No mapped test exists (Tasks).
